# Cloudflare Pages routing rules.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>
# Status 200 = rewrite (URL bar unchanged) — but Cloudflare Pages doesn't
#              reliably honor this when the source uses a wildcard/splat;
#              the .html-stripping canonicalizer turns the rewrite back
#              into a redirect and drops the splat. See:
#              https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
# Status 301/302 = redirect (URL bar changes to `to`)

# Shareable seller profile URLs: canvascircle.art/@handle
#
# We redirect (not rewrite) to /seller?handle=<handle>. The shareable URL
# the seller copies/posts stays /@handle — only the URL bar updates AFTER
# someone clicks it. seller.html reads the handle from the ?handle= query
# string (with the /@handle pathname form as a fallback).
#
# :splat captures the wildcard match and substitutes it into the destination.
/@*  /seller?handle=:splat  302
